// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// Niri fragment: Monitors / outputs (optional)
// Not included by default: niri auto-detects outputs, and a hardcoded panel
// name/scale is wrong on most boxes. Uncomment the include in config.kdl if
// you need a specific mode, scale, or VRR setting. Keep this file to pure
// `output { }` blocks and comments so it stays easy to replace per machine.
//
// The example below is for a 2880x1920@120 2x HiDPI laptop panel (eDP-1).
// Run: niri msg outputs — then rename the output line and set your values.
// Commented alternatives show the options; uncomment the lines you want.
// Per-output settings you can set:
//   mode "2880x1920@120"        // WIDTHxHEIGHT@REFRESH — resolution + refresh rate
//   scale 2                     // UI scaling: 1.0 native, 1.25/1.5/2 for sharper/fractional
//   variable-refresh-rate       // VRR: match refresh to content (reduces tearing)
//   position x=0 y=0            // Arrange multi-monitor layout
//   transform "90"              // Rotation: "90"/"180"/"270" (e.g. portrait second screen)
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────
output "eDP-1" {
    scale 2
    // mode "2880x1920@120"
    // variable-refresh-rate
    // position x=0 y=0
}
// Desktop / second monitor example (commented — enable by editing):
// output "DP-1" {
//     scale 1
//     // mode "2560x1440@144"
//     // variable-refresh-rate
// }
// Save → niri live-reloads (or: niri msg action load-config-file). Scale is
// fractional; VRR only kicks in if the panel + cable support it.
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────